ning hook and the following sushi-prep beats are too visually similar in tone and composition, making the transition feel repetitive rather than escalating.","fix":"Follow the hook with a clearly different angle or action beat to create contrast, then return to product detail later."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"CTA","timestamp_seconds":13.5,"problem":"The final on-screen message is not instantly understood as a visit prompt; it reads like a product caption rather than an actionable invitation.","fix":"Rewrite the end text to explicitly say where to go and when: KAIRO Sushi, Athens. Come taste the difference tonight."}]
